/P 331 0 R
/E (In sum, the absence of reliable, comprehensive, and standardized data across ASEAN countries remains a foundational challenge. It undermines the ability of governments, researchers, and development partners to track progress, identify gaps, and design targeted, responsive policies. If the goal of inclusive digital transformation is to be achieved, closing this data deficit must be a top priority. Investment in national statistical systems, adoption of common definitions, and coordinated regional efforts to ensure regular and gender-sensitive ICT data collection will be essential to drive informed action and achieve equitable outcomes in the digital economy.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [3 4]
>>
