/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 352 0 R
/T (This enrollment pattern warrants policy attention, though it should be interpreted alongside other contextual factors. The decline in female enrollment may reflect multiple influences including: limited exposure to ICT in earlier education, fewer visible role models in technical careers, perceptions of workplace culture in tech sectors, and individual career preferences formed through educational experiences. While these trends are consistent with the presence of barriers to entry, tertiary enrollment also reflects student agency in career selection based on their assessment of opportunities and fit.)
/E (This enrollment pattern warrants policy attention, though it should be interpreted alongside other contextual factors. The decline in female enrollment may reflect multiple influences including: limited exposure to ICT in earlier education, fewer visible role models in technical careers, perceptions of workplace culture in tech sectors, and individual career preferences formed through educational experiences. While these trends are consistent with the presence of barriers to entry, tertiary enrollment also reflects student agency in career selection based on their assessment of opportunities and fit.)
/Pg 49 0 R
/K [3]
>>
